{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_293","type":"agent_message","text":"Implementation complete. Final structured result:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"summary\": \"E01 reliability aggregation landed in the existing Agent Dev benefit report (no new metrics platform). Added scripts/lib/reliability-aggregation.mjs (pure, deterministic pass^k / pass@k / per-trial success / flake / anchor / safety aggregation), its .d.mts typing surface, the pre-registered fixture shared/agent-dev/reliability-fixture.json (k=3, minCases=20, flakeThreshold=0.01), and wired report.reliability plus a markdown block into scripts/agent-dev-benefit-eval.mjs. pass^k (0.25) and pass@k (0.75) are separate fields and never mixed; the timeout case is preserved as incomplete and excluded from denominators; flake is first-trial-fail-then-pass with the first failure kept; positive/negative anchor and safety-required violations force gate=fail; 4 complete cases < 20 yields gate=insufficient-sample, never PASS. Added the task spec, boundary rule, closure doc, e01-acceptance.json (agent-driven, explicitly deterministic-oracle, liveProvider=false, realHuman=false, productLocks.changed=false) and E01-SHA256SUMS (8/8 re-read OK). READMEs reviewed in all four locales and intentionally left byte-unchanged since this packet only adds an internal evaluation report block. No product default, product lock, approval semantics or scheduled automation changed. Note: the sealed oracle test path was never created or read; typecheck:test, the repo-wide manifest verifier and spec-lifecycle checks fail identically on the untouched base tree due to missing installed dependencies and pre-existing drift, so they are recorded as pre-existing rather than as passes.\",\n  \"testsRun\": [\n    \"node --check scripts/agent-dev-benefit-eval.mjs -> exit 0\",\n    \"node --check scripts/lib/reliability-aggregation.mjs -> exit 0\",\n    \"node -e fixture load of shared/agent-dev/reliability-fixture.json -